course: dictionary
lesson: 8204
title: Retelling a story
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To retell a story is to tell it again, often in your own words. You keep the main events, but you choose your own way of saying them. «Retell in your own words» means you do not copy the book word for word.
explain: Order matters when you retell. A recount retells real events in time order, so use clue words like «first», «then», «after that» and «finally». «On Tuesday, Class 4 went to the seaside. First, they paddled. Then they had lunch. Finally, they went home.» Your listener can follow it because the events come in the right order.
explain: A retelling can also be a new version of an old story. A modern retelling of a fairy tale might set it in a school or a space station, but the main events stay the same. Stories can keep real memories and still change. «Stories often grow each time they are retold» because each teller adds or stretches a little.
fact: Retell means to tell a story again.
fact: A retelling is a new version of an old story.
fact: A recount retells real events in time order, usually in the past tense.
fact: Time words like «first», «then», «after that» and «finally» show the order of events.
fact: Stories can keep real memories but change as they are retold, so a retelling is not always exactly what happened.
exercise: In a recount, what helps you retell events in the right order? | Question marks | *Time words like first, then and finally | Rhyming words | Adjectives like big and shiny
exercise: «Stories often grow each time they are retold.» What does this suggest? | *Stories can change a little each time someone tells them | Stories never get told again | Stories are only written down | Stories are always exactly the same
exercise: A «modern retelling» of a fairy tale is what? | A copy of the same book | A story with no ending | A diary of today's weather | *A new version of an old story
test: Which word means to tell a story again? | *Retell | Remember | Rewrap | Repaint
test: Which sentence is a recount? | Dragons are big and can breathe fire. | Please close the door when you leave. | I think the best colour is blue. | *First we walked to the shop, then we bought bread, and finally we went home.
exam: Why should you put events in time order when you retell a true story? | So you do not need to remember anything | So the story is always changed | *So the listener can follow what happened, step by step | So the story becomes longer and more exciting
